1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:12,900
Seven Transects is a playable WebMCP test for supervising a browser agent. We have seven scans to map half of this island at 88 percent precision.

2
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:34,900
This recording machine has Chrome 145, so the orange badge correctly reports that native WebMCP is off. The deployed page still registers six tools through document model context. In ChatGPT's browser or Chrome 149 and later, those definitions appear as Site tools.

3
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:50,600
For this review cut, I use the labeled local replay. It invokes the same production handlers while marking every event as local replay. The first calls read the objective, budgets, committed chart, and previous handoffs.

4
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:05,500
Survey region is a scarce write action. It spends one of seven charges and returns exact terrain along a narrow cross. The typed result updates the same chart the person is viewing.

5
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:33,300
The next tool stages a patch with exact cells and one cautious inference. It cannot commit the chart. I choose Accept verified, which keeps completed scan evidence and authorized human readings. Runtime checks reject an agent that labels an unsurveyed cell as exact.

6
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:58,400
For an uncertain diagonal, the agent requests human attention at one coordinate. I interpret the field layer and send a structured answer. Inspect chart gives that authorized answer back to the agent, so the handoff becomes part of the shared state.

7
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:22,200
A safety check costs one of two consultations. It returns a broad precision band without identifying correct cells or mistakes. This keeps the check useful without turning it into an answer oracle.

8
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:40,200
Later turns repeat the same review loop. Seven scans cover 60 unique cells. Human readings and manual chart decisions fill the remaining gaps while the trace keeps each source visible.

9
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:54,900
This run finishes at 50 percent coverage and 90 percent precision. The live app and public source are ready. Native Site tools capture is the last submission check.
